<div class="boilerplate metadata" style="border:1px solid #a66;padding:0.5em"><strong>Historical reference:</strong> The World Editor package is not among the two mods currently included in the ShroudForge repository's <code>mods/</code> folder. This page documents the former package and its settings.</div>

The World Editor was designed to copy, rotate, save, and paste parts of an Enshrouded world. Its historical package ID was <code>world-editor</code>. It targeted the client and Dedicated Server and declared 37 player settings.

The former package could capture voxel-and-prop or props-only blueprints, preview and paste them, and undo supported operations. Its settings covered the in-game panel, blueprint limits, entity placement, target position, rotation, and blueprint names.

Those details describe the archived package. They do not mean that the World Editor is currently shipped or supported as a bundled ShroudForge mod. Check the [https://github.com/bonsaibauer/shroudforge/tree/HEAD/mods current repository packages] and release notes for current contents.

